.TH TOMATOPLAY 1 "September 2026" "tomatoplay 1.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tomatoplay, tp \- browse and watch anime, movies, and TV series from multiple sources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tomatoplay
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
.br
.B tp
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tomatoplay
is a CLI tool to search and stream anime, movies, and TV series from multiple
sources. It provides interactive search via fzf/rofi/dmenu, quality selection,
download support, and a watch history. Run without arguments to get a home
menu: search, continue watching, history, trending, a surprise pick, or local
file playback. Pass an existing file or folder path to play it directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -s, --source SOURCE
Specify source: all, anidb, aniwatch, gogoanime, 9anime, animeplanet, anisearch, youtube, bilibili, nyaa.
.TP
.B nyaa
Search and play anime torrents from nyaa.si. Streams straight into mpv via
\fBwebtorrent-cli\fR (install with \fBnpm install -g webtorrent-cli\fR); without
it, the magnet is printed, copied to the clipboard, and the
.B .torrent
saved, so you can open it in any client.
.TP
.B -c, --continue
Continue watching from history, resuming where you left off — no audio or preview prompts (mpv).
.TP
.B -f, --file [PATH]
Play media from a local file or folder, fully offline — no search or network
needed. A folder path opens a picker; a file path starts playing immediately;
a bare path argument behaves the same. External subtitle files next to the
video are picked up automatically by the player.
.TP
.B -T, --trending
Browse what's popular right now, without typing a search.
.TP
.B -L, --lucky-tomato
Pluck a random (playable) show off the vine and start playing it.
.TP
.B -d, --download
Download the video instead of playing it.
.TP
.B -D, --delete
Delete history.
.TP
.B -H, --history
Print the watch history (episode per series).
.TP
.B --stats
Show watch stats harvested from history: series count, episodes logged,
approximate watch time, and the marathon champ.
.TP
.B --sources
Probe each source end-to-end (search, episode list, stream) and report which
ones are working right now. Results are cached.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_PROXY
Set a proxy (e.g. \fBTOMATOPLAY_PROXY=socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080\fR) applied to
every provider request. Needed for bilibili outside allowed regions; a system
VPN works too since curl already follows it.
.TP
.B -q, --quality
Specify the video quality.
.TP
.B -v, --vlc
Use VLC to play the video.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show the version of the script.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.TP
.B -e, --episode, -r, --range
Specify the number of episodes to watch (e.g. 5, or 1-10).
.TP
.B -a, --audio AUDIO
Choose the audio track for the current episode: \fBsub\fR (subtitled,
Japanese) or \fBdub\fR (English dub). When unset and the series has an
English dub, you will be asked interactively after picking an episode;
selecting another audio (where available) hides the prompt. Use
\fBchange_audio\fR in the playback menu to switch during playback.
.TP
.B --dub
Play the English dubbed version (same as \fB-a dub\fR).
.TP
.B --rofi
Use rofi instead of fzf for the interactive menu.
.TP
.B --dmenu
Use dmenu instead of fzf for the interactive menu.
.TP
.B --no-detach
Don't detach the player (useful for in-terminal playback, mpv only).
.TP
.B --exit-after-play
Exit the player and return the player exit code.
.TP
.B -n, --next
Marathon mode: after a show ends, automatically start the next episode and
keep going to the finale (implies \fB--no-detach\fR).
.TP
.B --preview
Peek at the first \fBTOMATOPLAY_PREVIEW_SECS\fR seconds (default 60) of an
episode before committing to a show. mpv only; implies \fB--no-detach\fR.
Also offered interactively after picking an episode (Esc skips it).
.TP
.B --cache-info
Show the cache directory, number of entries, and total size.
.TP
.B --clear-cache
Wipe the cache and start fresh.
.TP
.B --no-cache
Disable the cache for this run.
.TP
.B -U, --update
Update the script.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_DEFAULT_SOURCE
Default source (default: all).
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_PLAYER
Default player.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_QUALITY
Default quality.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Download directory.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_MENU
Menu program (fzf, rofi, dmenu).
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_MODE
Default audio track (sub, dub). Acts the same as passing \fB-a\fR.
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_PREVIEW_SECS
Preview length in seconds for \fB--preview\fR (default: 60).
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_CONFIG
Path to the config file (default: \fI~/.config/tomato-play/tomato-playrc\fR).
.TP
.B TOMATOPLAY_RESUME_BACK
Seconds rewound when resuming a partially-watched episode (default: 10).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Home menu (interactive)
.B tp
.TP
Search all sources for naruto
.B tp naruto
.TP
Search a specific source
.B tp -s gogoanime "one punch"
.TP
Watch specific episodes
.B tp -e 1-10 "one piece"
.TP
Download episodes
.B tp -d "naruto" -e 1-10
.SH DEPENDENCIES
curl, grep, sed, mpv or vlc, yt-dlp or ffmpeg, fzf.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/tomatoplay/history
Watch history.
.TP
.B ~/.config/tomato-play/tomato-playrc
Optional KEY=VALUE config file for defaults (mode, quality, player, menu,
source, download_dir, log, cache_ttl, resume_back). Precedence is CLI flags >
environment > config file. A commented starter is created on first run.
